#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:1
msgid "VTK::RenderingWebGPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:3
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:5
msgid ""
"This module contains the WebGPU native backend for `RenderingCore`. "
"Currently, it supports rendering polygonal geometry in different "
"representations with point/cell scalar-mapped colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:7
msgid ""
"When both the `RenderingOpenGL2` and `RenderingWebGPU` libraries are linked, "
"the user must provide preferences to select the rendering backend at "
"runtime. This can be done in two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:8
msgid ""
"Pass command line arguments to your application `--vtk-factory-prefer "
"RenderingBackend=WebGPU` or `--vtk-factory-prefer RenderingBackend=OpenGL2`. "
"Then, you will need to invoke "
"`vtkObjectFactory::InitializePreferencesFromCommandLineArgs(argc, argv)` in "
"your main function before creating any VTK object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:9
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set the `VTK_FACTORY_PREFER` environment variable to "
"`RenderingBackend=WebGPU` or `RenderingBackend=OpenGL2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:13
msgid "Building VTK with Dawn (Highly Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:15
msgid ""
"Dawn is optional. `VTK_ENABLE_WEBGPU=ON` builds this module against the "
"standard WebGPU C API and resolves the entry points at runtime, so Dawn does "
"not have to be installed to configure or build VTK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:19
msgid ""
"Set `VTK_USE_DAWN_WEBGPU=ON` to declare Dawn's own WebGPU extensions, which "
"go beyond the standard API (see [Standard WebGPU Headers](#standard-webgpu-"
"headers)). That option makes Dawn a hard requirement: point `Dawn_DIR` at "
"the installation, and configuration fails with an error if Dawn cannot be "
"found there. The option is unavailable on Emscripten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:25
msgid ""
"Leaving it `OFF` does not stop a Dawn library from being loaded at runtime; "
"it only means the extensions are not declared. The rest of this section "
"builds a Dawn and configures with those extensions enabled."
msgstr ""

